# FRONTEND · what must not enter the build context
#
# Short and hand-kept on purpose: everything in fl_frontend/ that is NOT listed here reaches the
# builder, so this list reads as an answer to "what does the image see?". Add a line when something
# new here is a secret, a machine-local artifact, or output the image rebuilds for itself.
#
# `**/` on anything that can appear at any depth: a bare pattern matches the context root ALONE, so
# `*.log` would leave src/**/*.log in the context. `**/` matches zero directories too, so the root
# copy is covered by the same line.

# Credentials, matched by shape rather than by inventory: each rule holds whether or not anything
# matches it right now, because a credential that reaches an image is a failure nobody sees until
# the image has shipped. The containers take their environment from compose's env_file at run time.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
# The deliberate trade in this block: an `.npmrc` more usually carries pnpm configuration than a
# credential, so one added later to shape the install would never reach `deps`, and the build would
# not say why. Excluded regardless -- a registry token is the other thing it holds, and a token
# inside a published image is found too late to matter. Anyone who needs an `.npmrc` in the build
# deletes this line knowing what it was for.
**/.npmrc

# Reinstalled by the deps stage from the lockfile, and the host tree is built for another platform,
# so copying it in would be both wrong and the largest thing in the context.
**/node_modules/

# Build output. The builder writes its own; the host's copy could only shadow it.
.next/

# Machine-local typechecker state (~700 KB, rewritten by every `pnpm typecheck`). In the context it
# makes the builder's `COPY . .` layer key depend on whether anyone ran the typechecker.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

**/*.log

# buildkit receives both by other means; copying them in only invalidates layers.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
